From: TYFZA1 native port <tyfza1@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: push flowtable encapsulations from inner to outer

flow_offload_fill_route stores encap[] in wire order, outermost first.
A VLAN_PUSH prepends a tag, so walking that array forward reverses QinQ
on hardware output. For FTTR this replaces the outer GEM service tag with
the customer's inner tag. Emit the output actions from inner to outer,
also placing PPPoE before its enclosing VLAN. Input pops remain forward.

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_offload.c
@@ -734,7 +734,8 @@ nf_flow_rule_route_common(struct net *net, const struct flow_offload *flow,
 
 	other_tuple = &flow->tuplehash[!dir].tuple;
 
-	for (i = 0; i < other_tuple->encap_num; i++) {
+	/* encap[] is outermost first; each push prepends to the packet. */
+	for (i = other_tuple->encap_num - 1; i >= 0; i--) {
 		struct flow_action_entry *entry;
 
 		if (other_tuple->in_vlan_ingress & BIT(i))
